WEBVTT

﻿1
00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

2
00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.776
Oh, that Ae-sun!

3
00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:10.361
- Whoa. Hey! Come on! Stop!
- That damn Ae-sun! Ae-sun, damn you!

4
00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:12.072
- Goodness, Mother.
- What did I do?

5
00:01:12.155 --> 00:01:14.783
- Please, Mother!
- I told your grandson no!

6
00:01:14.866 --> 00:01:17.077
- That child!
- I said, "No, thank you." All right?

7
00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.579
- That damn girl! Ae-sun!
- Oh my God!

8
00:01:19.662 --> 00:01:21.915
Nana, why are you doing this? Why, why?

9
00:01:21.998 --> 00:01:23.541
What?

10
00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:27.504
Tell me why you'd ruin
someone else's cabbages like that.

11
00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.380
Why, you little…

12
00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:32.258
She said, "No, thanks. No, thank you."

13
00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:55.240
Barnacles and conches.

14
00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.869
A <i>haenyeo's </i>daughter
and a fish seller's son.

15
00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:01.788
Same difference.

16
00:02:02.872 --> 00:02:04.874
It's not like you are nobility.

17
00:02:26.563 --> 00:02:29.274
Nothing will happen
just 'cause we hang out.

18
00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.944
Yeah, I mean, I simply wanna sit
next to somebody's store

19
00:02:33.027 --> 00:02:34.696
so I can run my family business.

20
00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:37.699
It's not like I'm obsessed
with finding a husband.

21
00:02:39.951 --> 00:02:41.828
I wouldn't get hitched to you anyway,

22
00:02:42.579 --> 00:02:43.955
even if they made me.

23
00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:45.081
I'm not crazy.

24
00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:48.126
Why would I marry an island guy?
All my roots are in Seoul.

25
00:02:48.209 --> 00:02:49.252
A store in Gyeonggi.

26
00:02:50.086 --> 00:02:51.462
Your uncle operates one.

27
00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:53.131
In Gyeonggi.

28
00:02:53.214 --> 00:02:54.799
Yeah, and Gyeonggi is nearly Seoul.

29
00:03:00.805 --> 00:03:03.099
Damn sea swallowed up
my mother and my father.

30
00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.977
Makes me sick seeing those waves
come from every direction.

31
00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.312
You think I'd settle here?

32
00:03:07.812 --> 00:03:10.940
I'm going to marry a man from Seoul,
no matter what.

33
00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.525
I won't marry an islander.

34
00:03:13.318 --> 00:03:17.071
Especially anyone that can't comprehend
what "nostalgia" is.

35
00:03:17.155 --> 00:03:18.239
Never!

36
00:03:21.618 --> 00:03:24.621
Cat got your tongue or what?
Why aren't you saying anything?

37
00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:28.208
God, I'd rather hang with
a <i>dolhareubang </i>statue.

38
00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:30.043
So take your hand out of my pocket

39
00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.128
since I'm not a guy from Seoul.

40
00:03:52.607 --> 00:03:54.400
Give away your son if you like.

41
00:03:55.109 --> 00:03:58.738
It sure looks like you're totally fine
giving him away to that girl.

42
00:03:59.322 --> 00:04:00.990
I'd never go against your word, would I?

43
00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.075
You would.

44
00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:04.827
You arrived knocked up.

45
00:04:05.328 --> 00:04:06.704
Don't be too harsh on them.

46
00:04:06.788 --> 00:04:09.999
It could make them go too far.
You know what I mean, right?

47
00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.627
I know.
That's why I was so darn mad.

48
00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:14.087
If we leave them alone,

49
00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.339
they'll run away
in the middle of the night

50
00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:18.549
right under your nose, just like you did.

51
00:04:18.633 --> 00:04:23.513
So you're saying that
I robbed you of your son, is that right?

52
00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:26.474
Rumors spread like wildfire
on a small island like ours.

53
00:04:26.557 --> 00:04:28.518
Everyone knows what you did back then.

54
00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.187
Why are you pretending to be
such a saint, huh?

55
00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:34.148
Well, he's just a teen.
They'll be together a bit and move on.

56
00:04:34.232 --> 00:04:35.775
Leave them alone.

57
00:04:35.858 --> 00:04:39.153
Once they've had enough, they'll stop.
Why is it so concerning to you?

58
00:04:39.237 --> 00:04:40.863
Not much we can do, you know.

59
00:04:41.364 --> 00:04:44.867
Yes, the sons in our two families
really have been idiots.

60
00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:49.455
They have been confused for generations,
and I'm the mean wench who's crazy.

61
00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.125
Leave them alone.

62
00:04:53.251 --> 00:04:56.504
He wouldn't bring a beggar in
just because he feels guilty, right?

63
00:04:56.587 --> 00:04:57.422
Hmm?

64
00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.685
Giving us seer fish today?

65
00:05:12.228 --> 00:05:13.771
Well, aren't we the lucky ones?

66
00:05:14.355 --> 00:05:16.524
Can't believe we get so many freebies.

67
00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:20.528
If I fed people I felt bad for,
I'd give that to a beggar.

68
00:05:21.029 --> 00:05:22.030
At school,

69
00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.866
you always used to give me
your leftover milk,

70
00:05:24.949 --> 00:05:27.160
and… I'm so damn grateful.

71
00:05:28.453 --> 00:05:30.872
You think I gave you fish
for ten years out of pity?

72
00:05:31.414 --> 00:05:33.333
So why do you do it?

73
00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:35.793
You think I'd be a moron for ten years?

74
00:05:36.294 --> 00:05:37.962
So why are you giving them to us?

75
00:05:38.755 --> 00:05:40.506
It's about damn time you told me.

76
00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:44.469
What are you looking at?

77
00:05:45.303 --> 00:05:47.638
Look me in the eye for once
and say something.

78
00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.684
You give me food
and never do anything else.

79
00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:56.064
What, your grandma say to give us fish
but to keep your mouth shut?

80
00:05:56.606 --> 00:05:58.733
Did she tell you not to waste your breath?

81
00:06:06.616 --> 00:06:08.409
Damn little runt of a man.

82
00:06:09.452 --> 00:06:11.204
You're such a brat.

83
00:06:14.123 --> 00:06:15.541
Do you kiss little runt men?

84
00:06:15.625 --> 00:06:16.751
That was my philtrum.

85
00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:18.294
I wouldn't kiss beggars either.

86
00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:20.213
Uh… Hold on, um,

87
00:06:20.797 --> 00:06:23.257
so you like me, is that it, huh?

88
00:06:23.341 --> 00:06:26.010
I want to be living with you.
Not… not with my grandma.

89
00:06:27.929 --> 00:06:28.971
Oh, um,

90
00:06:29.764 --> 00:06:32.308
but why would you kiss my philtrum,

91
00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:33.976
and after I, well--

92
00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.353
Oh my God, just shut up already!

93
00:06:35.937 --> 00:06:38.606
What's with you? Your mouth is going,
and you keep saying things,

94
00:06:38.689 --> 00:06:40.817
and I have no idea
what you're talking about.

95
00:06:41.317 --> 00:06:44.153
You're the brat who puts her hand
in my pocket. What am I supposed to say?

96
00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:46.447
- What's with your glossy lips every day?
- I wear lipstick!

97
00:06:46.531 --> 00:06:47.490
- Why?
- So I'm ready.

98
00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:48.699
Uh, what?

99
00:06:49.492 --> 00:06:50.910
Oh shit.

100
00:06:51.661 --> 00:06:54.914
I've been ready since I was 14, and, uh…

101
00:07:18.896 --> 00:07:22.024
<i>The Jeju Canola Flower Festival</i>
<i>has begun once again.</i>

102
00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:25.403
{\an8}<i>Jeju Island is bustling with tourists</i>
<i>who've gathered to see the scenery</i>

103
00:07:25.486 --> 00:07:26.904
{\an8}<i>embellished with canola flowers.</i>

104
00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.157
<i>Today, there are a great variety</i>

105
00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.617
<i>of interesting events</i>
<i>planned for couples as well.</i>

106
00:07:31.701 --> 00:07:33.995
<i>So let's interview some of the visitors.</i>

107
00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.457
<i>Hello, would you mind</i>
<i>if I asked a few questions?</i>

108
00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:40.168
- <i>No problem.</i>
<i>- So you're here to see the flowers today.</i>

109
00:07:40.251 --> 00:07:41.544
{\an8}<i>How do you feel about it?</i>

110
00:07:42.211 --> 00:07:43.045
<i>Well…</i>

111
00:07:43.671 --> 00:07:46.132
<i>The flowers remind me of my first love.</i>

112
00:07:46.215 --> 00:07:48.593
<i>Oh, your first love.</i>
<i>Of course, yes, yes.</i>

113
00:07:48.676 --> 00:07:49.969
<i>Go live with her, then.</i>

114
00:07:51.053 --> 00:07:51.888
<i>Oh…</i>

115
00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:53.264
<i>Oh, Hye-ran. No, no.</i>

116
00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:56.893
Mom, is Dad your first love?

117
00:07:57.935 --> 00:07:59.520
Was he your first love?

118
00:08:00.354 --> 00:08:01.856
I don't know.

119
00:08:01.939 --> 00:08:03.274
Yeah, I've forgotten.

120
00:08:03.858 --> 00:08:05.526
Was he your first kiss?

121
00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:08.821
Idiot! Hey, Mom doesn't need that.

122
00:08:09.405 --> 00:08:11.365
You gotta be crazy
to ask a question like that.

123
00:08:11.449 --> 00:08:13.326
- Shut up.
- You little…

124
00:08:13.409 --> 00:08:14.952
- <i>So beautiful.</i>
- <i>Yes.</i>

125
00:08:15.036 --> 00:08:17.663
<i>More beautiful than</i>
<i>the ones in our city.</i>

126
00:08:17.747 --> 00:08:20.458
Did you know canola flowers
smell really intense?

127
00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:25.004
The smell's sweet and really intense.

128
00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:29.592
And the headache you get,
you… you feel like fainting.

129
00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:37.850
I'm hungry.

130
00:08:38.726 --> 00:08:40.978
Why haven't you eaten anything yet?

131
00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:44.398
God, can't you just
get rid of this thing here?

132
00:08:44.941 --> 00:08:46.901
Oh, dinner will be done in a jiffy.

133
00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:56.202
Why would you watch that?
That's so boring.

134
00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:57.620
<i>The expo…</i>

135
00:09:00.623 --> 00:09:01.624
{\an8}Oh.

136
00:09:01.707 --> 00:09:03.709
{\an8}MARINATED CHICKEN

137
00:09:11.425 --> 00:09:15.221
<i>Had I known that</i>
<i>spring was truly the spring of my life,</i>

138
00:09:16.514 --> 00:09:20.309
<i>I would've dared</i>
<i>to give myself to love even more.</i>

139
00:09:21.602 --> 00:09:23.354
I still won't marry you.

140
00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:29.902
Oh, today, uh…

141
00:09:30.444 --> 00:09:32.863
Today, the, uh, practice was really tough.

142
00:09:32.947 --> 00:09:34.282
Shut up and walk.

143
00:09:59.557 --> 00:10:06.564
<i>♪ That boy, Sun-bong</i>
<i>Who walks home at eight o'clock ♪</i>

144
00:10:07.982 --> 00:10:14.989
<i>♪ Will I get to see him tomorrow?</i>
<i>I look forward to it ♪</i>

145
00:10:16.616 --> 00:10:19.994
<i>♪ Sun-nam was eating ♪</i>

146
00:10:20.536 --> 00:10:24.081
<i>♪ And now she's gone ♪</i>

147
00:10:26.042 --> 00:10:29.003
<i>♪ Sun-nam was eating ♪</i>

148
00:10:30.171 --> 00:10:33.883
<i>♪ And now she's hiding ♪</i>

149
00:10:33.966 --> 00:10:35.176
I found you!

150
00:10:37.428 --> 00:10:39.597
<i>But spring was ever so fickle.</i>

151
00:10:49.607 --> 00:10:52.193
<i>Just when it felt warm, it would get cold.</i>

152
00:10:54.654 --> 00:10:57.281
<i>Just when it felt cold, it would get hot.</i>

153
00:11:00.076 --> 00:11:02.662
<i>It never ceases to keep you guessing.</i>

154
00:11:08.209 --> 00:11:09.293
We did nothing wrong.

155
00:11:11.212 --> 00:11:12.296
Min-ok.

156
00:11:16.133 --> 00:11:19.470
Morally, I'm a virgin. A virgin.

157
00:11:20.096 --> 00:11:22.932
Legally speaking, I'm single,
so no problem there.

158
00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:24.100
Min-ok.

159
00:11:24.767 --> 00:11:27.770
Why should I need to play caretaker
to your dead wife's kids?

160
00:11:28.354 --> 00:11:30.231
Why do you act like
someone's lording over you?

161
00:11:30.314 --> 00:11:32.066
Why are you saving face constantly?

162
00:11:32.149 --> 00:11:33.859
Next year, you'll be-- You will-- Huh?

163
00:11:33.943 --> 00:11:35.736
Whoa! Whoa!

164
00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:42.952
Are you someone's puppet?

165
00:12:03.848 --> 00:12:07.393
Mom, Jong-gu is your eldest grandson.

166
00:12:07.476 --> 00:12:09.729
No matter where you look
in our family tree,

167
00:12:09.812 --> 00:12:12.106
he'll lead ancestral rites
when you're gone.

168
00:12:13.983 --> 00:12:14.984
What?

169
00:12:15.693 --> 00:12:16.944
Something troubling you?

170
00:12:17.737 --> 00:12:19.071
So what if it is?

171
00:12:19.155 --> 00:12:22.742
You've been taking care of that family.
Now you want something from us?

172
00:12:24.034 --> 00:12:26.203
Grandma, don't you have your own room?

173
00:12:26.996 --> 00:12:28.831
You all eat and sleep in that one room?

174
00:12:28.914 --> 00:12:31.208
Well, if your family's in this state,

175
00:12:31.292 --> 00:12:34.086
the least you can do is
work at a factory or something

176
00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:36.672
and provide for this family.
Why are you helping them?

177
00:12:38.966 --> 00:12:40.634
Do they pay you enough for this work?

178
00:12:41.218 --> 00:12:44.638
I'm not making a living.
This is just so I can buy sweets.

179
00:12:44.722 --> 00:12:45.848
And… and what was that?

180
00:12:45.931 --> 00:12:48.184
Are you a literary girl
yearning for college?

181
00:12:48.267 --> 00:12:50.186
Jong-gu never even went to college.

182
00:12:52.188 --> 00:12:53.022
What?

183
00:12:54.231 --> 00:12:55.900
Do you wanna go to college?

184
00:12:57.818 --> 00:13:01.113
Mom, do you have savings
to give her when we're in this state?

185
00:13:01.197 --> 00:13:02.406
Get paid by your other family.

186
00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:04.450
They should pay you
so you can pay for college.

187
00:13:04.533 --> 00:13:05.951
You're their housekeeper.

188
00:13:06.035 --> 00:13:08.954
If we had spoiled rice,
we wouldn't give it to a dog.

189
00:13:09.038 --> 00:13:10.247
Ow!

190
00:13:11.957 --> 00:13:13.459
Why would you take this down?

191
00:13:13.542 --> 00:13:15.836
It's not yours to take down.
Why did you touch this picture?

192
00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.630
- It's not yours!
- What did you expect?

193
00:13:17.713 --> 00:13:20.633
You thought I'd have a picture
of his ex-wife over my head?

194
00:13:21.717 --> 00:13:24.887
Sun-nam, Sun-bong, where were you
when she took down Mom's picture?

195
00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.597
How can you eat those right now?

196
00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:28.849
You see this girl
dividing the family?

197
00:13:28.933 --> 00:13:31.560
She's already working them
to be on her side.

198
00:13:32.394 --> 00:13:34.230
You shouldn't have
only bought four ice pops.

199
00:13:34.313 --> 00:13:36.232
- Okay?
- And why would I get five?

200
00:13:36.315 --> 00:13:39.151
- Why suck up to your ex-wife's daughter?
- Min-ok.

201
00:13:39.235 --> 00:13:42.696
Just forget it.
Please tell me you have some sense left.

202
00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:44.156
Min-ok.

203
00:13:44.949 --> 00:13:47.576
That's okay. Just let it go.
Give me my money.

204
00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.246
If you do,
I'll leave even if you tell me to stay.

205
00:13:50.329 --> 00:13:51.163
Wait.

206
00:13:51.831 --> 00:13:54.416
No. You borrowed money from a child?

207
00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:55.417
Min-ok.

208
00:13:56.335 --> 00:13:57.211
For what purpose?

209
00:13:57.294 --> 00:14:00.381
- I would never--
- I want the tuition money right now.

210
00:14:00.464 --> 00:14:03.467
You said if I raised your kids,
you'd send me to college.

211
00:14:04.593 --> 00:14:05.678
Oh.

212
00:14:06.804 --> 00:14:08.848
He gave you a home
when you had nowhere to go.

213
00:14:08.931 --> 00:14:10.474
Now you want a sack of cash too?

214
00:14:11.183 --> 00:14:13.269
Give me my money. You promised.

215
00:14:14.186 --> 00:14:15.896
And I even sold your cabbages too.

216
00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:17.106
Why won't you pay me?

217
00:14:17.773 --> 00:14:21.193
You said you'd be too scared of Mom
and that you'd never con me.

218
00:14:21.277 --> 00:14:22.903
Why would he be
afraid of a dead wife?

219
00:14:22.987 --> 00:14:25.030
He should be more scared
of his kids growing fast.

220
00:14:25.114 --> 00:14:26.198
Min-ok.

221
00:14:26.282 --> 00:14:29.869
Next year, by this time,
he'll have three to take care of.

222
00:14:29.952 --> 00:14:31.954
Why would he pay for your tuition?

223
00:14:32.663 --> 00:14:36.792
More importantly, Byeong-cheol
barely has enough cash to provide for us.

224
00:14:36.876 --> 00:14:40.963
Rumor has it he lives with me
because he can't pay me what he owes.

225
00:14:41.046 --> 00:14:43.048
- Na Min-ok.
- What? Damn you, Byeong-cheol!

226
00:14:43.132 --> 00:14:44.717
Sh! Sh.

227
00:14:50.764 --> 00:14:53.267
Get it, my dear? He had you fooled.

228
00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:56.395
See, you're… on your own, Ae-sun.

229
00:14:59.189 --> 00:15:01.859
Of course you're on your own now.
What'd you expect?

230
00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:07.323
In life,
you learn it's every man for himself.

231
00:15:07.406 --> 00:15:09.491
Right now,
best thing is learning to solder.

232
00:15:09.575 --> 00:15:13.454
They teach you the skill, they feed you,
they pay you, and you're a patriot.

233
00:15:13.537 --> 00:15:15.497
There's no better opportunity
for you than this.

234
00:15:15.581 --> 00:15:19.001
{\an8}And see, it's on the mainland,
just like you always wanted.

235
00:15:21.378 --> 00:15:23.839
If you work like a dog for a few years,

236
00:15:23.923 --> 00:15:26.091
they'll pay you 15,000 won a month.

237
00:15:26.175 --> 00:15:27.885
And if you live at the factory,

238
00:15:27.968 --> 00:15:29.678
you won't have to spend any money.

239
00:15:30.763 --> 00:15:31.639
So you

240
00:15:32.181 --> 00:15:35.351
send us back half the money
each month, all right?

241
00:15:35.434 --> 00:15:37.227
Every single month. Hmm?

242
00:15:40.189 --> 00:15:42.650
The eldest grandson
in the family's debt is yours.

243
00:15:42.733 --> 00:15:45.486
Jong-gu has to do well
for you to find a husband.

244
00:15:48.739 --> 00:15:52.451
You know, Mom said it's easier
to… to just be a cow…

245
00:15:54.495 --> 00:15:56.246
than to be a girl in Jeju.

246
00:15:58.374 --> 00:16:01.085
Jong-gu's been holding
ancestral rites for your father.

247
00:16:01.669 --> 00:16:04.004
Don't talk of things you don't understand.

248
00:16:04.088 --> 00:16:06.173
Oh, Jong-gu's rice is getting cold.

249
00:16:06.256 --> 00:16:07.675
I won't work there.

250
00:16:08.759 --> 00:16:09.593
I won't do it.

251
00:16:11.553 --> 00:16:14.306
I won't take care of
your family or my siblings.

252
00:16:15.474 --> 00:16:16.308
No one.

253
00:16:16.392 --> 00:16:18.352
If you won't work,
where will you go, then?

254
00:16:18.936 --> 00:16:22.064
You wanna live in this tiny house
and add to our worries?

255
00:16:22.648 --> 00:16:24.817
I won't do that. Any of it.

256
00:16:25.818 --> 00:16:27.987
If I keep living like an idiot,
it'll make…

257
00:16:29.863 --> 00:16:31.156
it'll make Mom cry.

258
00:16:34.535 --> 00:16:35.577
Ae-sun,

259
00:16:36.578 --> 00:16:37.579
think it through.

260
00:16:38.414 --> 00:16:39.873
Your mom is gone for good.

261
00:16:41.333 --> 00:16:42.167
Huh?

262
00:16:42.876 --> 00:16:44.294
You won't be

263
00:16:45.045 --> 00:16:47.381
welcome anywhere in the world.

264
00:17:12.322 --> 00:17:13.991
How many rooms are in your house?

265
00:17:14.491 --> 00:17:17.119
Your grandmother's word is law, right?

266
00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:20.372
It is, yeah? It is, right?

267
00:17:22.124 --> 00:17:24.293
What… what happened to you?
Who… who upset you?

268
00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:26.295
"Go to Busan," he said!

269
00:17:27.171 --> 00:17:29.256
He told me to go work at a factory.

270
00:17:29.965 --> 00:17:31.800
I don't have a home anymore.

271
00:17:32.551 --> 00:17:34.845
Sun-nam and Sun-bong took popsicles

272
00:17:35.512 --> 00:17:39.349
from that woman,
and my grandma's family is broke.

273
00:17:40.684 --> 00:17:41.935
And I'm not wanted

274
00:17:42.728 --> 00:17:44.354
anywhere anymore.

275
00:17:45.481 --> 00:17:47.733
The only one who even cares about me,

276
00:17:48.442 --> 00:17:50.611
the only one has to be you, Yang Gwan-sik.

277
00:17:51.445 --> 00:17:52.738
So…

278
00:17:55.532 --> 00:17:57.159
Why me?

279
00:17:57.242 --> 00:18:00.162
Why is it a boy from this island?

280
00:18:07.795 --> 00:18:09.463
<i>There's an outcry with no sound</i>

281
00:18:10.547 --> 00:18:12.925
<i>An eternal handkerchief of nostalgia</i>

282
00:18:13.008 --> 00:18:15.052
<i>That waves</i>
<i>That waves towards the blue sea</i>

283
00:18:16.053 --> 00:18:19.014
<i>I'm going to marry a man</i>
<i>from Seoul, no matter what.</i>

284
00:18:19.098 --> 00:18:22.017
<i>A true heart like a wave, flaps</i>

285
00:18:23.018 --> 00:18:26.146
<i>A true heart flaps like a wave</i>
<i>Just like the wind</i>

286
00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:30.359
I'd never marry a man who doesn't know
what "nostalgia" is. Never!

287
00:18:30.984 --> 00:18:32.611
<i>The first man hanging</i>
<i>In the air</i>

288
00:18:33.946 --> 00:18:35.447
<i>Ah, who is he?</i>

289
00:18:36.031 --> 00:18:38.158
<i>Suspended in the air, the first man</i>

290
00:18:38.242 --> 00:18:40.452
<i>With a blue</i>
<i>And bitter, bitter heart inside</i>

291
00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:44.289
Who cares if you know
what "nostalgia" means?

292
00:18:45.082 --> 00:18:47.793
What about college?
What about being a poet?

293
00:18:47.876 --> 00:18:49.503
And the mainland?

294
00:18:52.256 --> 00:18:53.340
I can't give you everything.

295
00:18:56.468 --> 00:18:57.594
But I'll do one thing,

296
00:18:58.178 --> 00:18:59.680
even if my life depends on it.

297
00:18:59.763 --> 00:19:03.183
Hey, can you at least just say that you'll

298
00:19:03.725 --> 00:19:05.644
give me everything?

299
00:19:05.727 --> 00:19:08.856
Tell me that you'll give me
the stars and the moon.

300
00:19:11.358 --> 00:19:14.236
How can I live with a boy like you?

301
00:19:15.362 --> 00:19:17.614
I don't know. I can't be a liar.

302
00:19:18.782 --> 00:19:23.203
You're actually scared
of your grandmother, too, aren't you?

303
00:19:30.252 --> 00:19:31.712
<i>This is an outcry with no sound</i>

304
00:19:31.795 --> 00:19:32.754
Oh, shut up.

305
00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:40.304
<i>There's an outcry with no sound</i>

306
00:19:40.387 --> 00:19:41.722
Stop it!

307
00:19:42.764 --> 00:19:44.683
<i>An eternal handkerchief of nostalgia</i>

308
00:19:45.684 --> 00:19:47.603
<i>That waves toward the blue sea</i>

309
00:20:03.785 --> 00:20:05.787
<i>You don't have to fight to win.</i>

310
00:20:07.497 --> 00:20:08.540
<i>The way I see it,</i>

311
00:20:08.624 --> 00:20:11.001
<i>even if you're a pro wrestler</i>
<i>like "Headbutting" Kim Il,</i>

312
00:20:11.084 --> 00:20:13.503
<i>it's better to avoid a punch</i>
<i>than to fight back.</i>

313
00:20:43.909 --> 00:20:45.786
<i>Even when we run away,</i>

314
00:20:45.869 --> 00:20:48.080
<i>we have to take what we're owed, don't we?</i>

315
00:20:54.253 --> 00:20:55.128
Sh.

316
00:21:23.782 --> 00:21:27.452
Your grandmother is going
to have me imprisoned for life.

317
00:21:44.219 --> 00:21:45.429
You sure you won't regret this?

318
00:21:46.179 --> 00:21:47.723
Because once we leave Jeju,

319
00:21:48.515 --> 00:21:50.517
there won't be any turning back anymore.

320
00:21:51.518 --> 00:21:53.312
Uh, damn it.

321
00:21:53.395 --> 00:21:55.522
You don't get
a second opportunity in life.

322
00:21:57.149 --> 00:22:00.402
If your life and my life
join together as one,

323
00:22:00.485 --> 00:22:02.654
we tough it out together,
whether we live or die.

324
00:22:06.283 --> 00:22:08.076
So if you're afraid, then go now.

325
00:22:09.995 --> 00:22:11.371
Just run home, okay?

326
00:22:15.584 --> 00:22:18.920
In the…19 years I've lived, I, uh…

327
00:22:23.508 --> 00:22:24.968
I've never felt this excited.

328
00:22:34.019 --> 00:22:36.521
- How fast is your 100 meters?
- Twenty-four seconds.

329
00:22:37.606 --> 00:22:38.815
All right. Let's go.

330
00:22:45.072 --> 00:22:47.699
<i>Who can stop spring</i>
<i>when it arrives inevitably?</i>

331
00:22:47.783 --> 00:22:50.619
FEMALE RUNAWAY PREVENTION PERIOD

332
00:22:50.702 --> 00:22:52.621
<i>Springtime in Jeju</i>

333
00:22:52.704 --> 00:22:54.706
<i>arrived particularly early</i>

334
00:22:55.540 --> 00:22:56.458
<i>that year.</i>

335
00:23:05.217 --> 00:23:07.302
<i>To celebrate</i>
<i>a springtime revolution,</i>

336
00:23:07.386 --> 00:23:09.262
<i>the May 16 military coup,</i>

337
00:23:09.346 --> 00:23:12.432
<i>all provinces of the nation</i>
<i>are preparing for festivals.</i>

338
00:23:12.516 --> 00:23:13.350
<i>For this…</i>

339
00:23:13.934 --> 00:23:15.310
<i>That spring,</i>

340
00:23:15.811 --> 00:23:19.314
<i>their coup, as ambitious</i>
<i>as their first voyage…</i>

341
00:23:19.856 --> 00:23:21.775
<i>The president</i>
<i>started a revolution</i>

342
00:23:21.858 --> 00:23:25.028
<i>when the nation needed protection from</i>
<i>Kim Shin-jo's team of North Korea.</i>

343
00:23:25.612 --> 00:23:28.073
<i>…wasn't as revolutionary as they'd hoped.</i>

344
00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:30.325
Provincial ID, please.

345
00:23:33.453 --> 00:23:35.080
Provincial ID.

346
00:23:36.331 --> 00:23:39.167
Without ID,
we'll consider you DPRK agents.

347
00:23:41.628 --> 00:23:44.172
You said you're both adults.
Let's see your IDs.

348
00:23:45.674 --> 00:23:48.009
Why do you look scared,
sitting in a corner like this?

349
00:23:48.510 --> 00:23:51.304
What are you saying? I don't understand.

350
00:23:53.265 --> 00:23:55.725
- Uh, sir.
- I think you're minors.

351
00:23:56.726 --> 00:23:59.688
Sir? We're not, um…

352
00:24:00.564 --> 00:24:01.982
You're both runaways, huh?

353
00:24:03.859 --> 00:24:06.319
How'd you end up together? Wow.

354
00:24:06.903 --> 00:24:10.115
Oh, what are you trying to say, sir?
I don't understand at all.

355
00:24:11.199 --> 00:24:13.994
Kids are so ballsy these days. Shit.

356
00:24:14.077 --> 00:24:16.246
How dare you
get on this ship by yourselves?

357
00:24:18.748 --> 00:24:19.666
So throw us over.

358
00:24:19.749 --> 00:24:20.584
What?

359
00:24:23.128 --> 00:24:24.421
Throw us overboard here.

360
00:24:25.839 --> 00:24:28.049
What makes you so brash?

361
00:24:28.133 --> 00:24:30.927
Is your family rich?
Is your father a politician or what?

362
00:24:33.847 --> 00:24:35.056
Throw us over.

363
00:24:36.641 --> 00:24:37.476
What's that?

364
00:24:38.185 --> 00:24:40.395
Come on, girl. What?

365
00:24:40.479 --> 00:24:42.147
What are you?

366
00:24:42.230 --> 00:24:43.356
Married.

367
00:24:46.067 --> 00:24:47.027
What?

368
00:24:47.944 --> 00:24:49.905
Husband and wife.

369
00:24:51.281 --> 00:24:54.284
We're married because we're adults.
How can kids get married?

370
00:24:54.868 --> 00:24:55.785
Let's go, babe.

371
00:25:22.479 --> 00:25:23.563
So what are you two?

372
00:25:24.189 --> 00:25:25.190
Husband and wife.

373
00:25:30.737 --> 00:25:32.072
What do I do with those?

374
00:25:32.155 --> 00:25:34.115
Why are you being so rude to us, ma'am?

375
00:25:34.783 --> 00:25:35.909
Are these really yours?

376
00:25:35.992 --> 00:25:37.994
Are people in Busan
typically this rude to customers?

377
00:25:38.078 --> 00:25:39.287
We're all adults here.

378
00:25:39.371 --> 00:25:41.998
- Did you steal these?
- They're his grandmother's rings.

379
00:25:51.007 --> 00:25:52.259
I need to see your IDs.

380
00:25:52.342 --> 00:25:53.176
We forgot them.

381
00:25:53.260 --> 00:25:56.680
Oh, yes, I'm sure.
You just forgot, yeah.

382
00:25:56.763 --> 00:26:00.767
- I was born in, uh, '49.
- That was the Year of the Tiger.

383
00:26:00.850 --> 00:26:02.894
- '49, Year of the Tiger.
- Year of the Ox, dear.

384
00:26:04.771 --> 00:26:06.773
What are these? You stole 'em or what?

385
00:26:08.191 --> 00:26:10.110
- Are you a thief, kid?
- We're runaways.

386
00:26:20.662 --> 00:26:22.914
NAMPOJANG INN

387
00:26:22.998 --> 00:26:25.166
We don't have a provincial ID

388
00:26:25.792 --> 00:26:27.419
or a national ID.

389
00:26:28.295 --> 00:26:31.089
We were robbed,

390
00:26:31.881 --> 00:26:34.009
so we don't have anything with us, unless…

391
00:26:35.927 --> 00:26:36.803
Take it out.

392
00:26:46.646 --> 00:26:48.690
Can you let us have a room for this?

393
00:26:50.692 --> 00:26:51.610
Guess not.

394
00:26:52.527 --> 00:26:55.405
Uh, you could see if a pawn shop wants it.

395
00:26:55.488 --> 00:26:56.489
Newlyweds?

396
00:26:57.824 --> 00:26:59.326
You look like newlyweds.

397
00:26:59.409 --> 00:27:01.161
Are you kids on your honeymoon?

398
00:27:03.121 --> 00:27:04.956
Huh. Hmm.

399
00:27:05.040 --> 00:27:06.207
No problem.

400
00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:07.667
You pay us tomorrow, okay?

401
00:27:07.751 --> 00:27:12.005
Wow, how kind of you.
Are we running a charity, dear?

402
00:27:12.088 --> 00:27:14.341
Their wallets were stolen
on their honeymoon.

403
00:27:14.424 --> 00:27:16.009
They must be so upset.

404
00:27:19.387 --> 00:27:21.556
Wait, are you giving us a room?

405
00:27:23.099 --> 00:27:25.018
Don't feel bad about being robbed here.

406
00:27:25.644 --> 00:27:28.188
Busan's hospitality is top-notch.

407
00:27:48.792 --> 00:27:50.752
You could voice your opinion, you know.

408
00:27:51.503 --> 00:27:53.129
You that scared of your grandma?

409
00:27:54.339 --> 00:27:55.548
I'm not afraid of her.

410
00:27:56.925 --> 00:28:00.845
Did she say you're naughty if you speak up
and then virtuous if you run away?

411
00:28:02.430 --> 00:28:04.099
I'm not afraid of my grandmother.

412
00:28:06.101 --> 00:28:07.143
Fine, you're not.

413
00:28:10.438 --> 00:28:12.607
I was afraid of her
giving you a hard time.

414
00:28:23.451 --> 00:28:27.122
Are you… okay with giving up on athletics?

415
00:28:28.498 --> 00:28:29.749
I'm not even that good.

416
00:28:31.584 --> 00:28:33.586
I only went 'cause you get milk and bread.

417
00:28:35.046 --> 00:28:36.339
What are you, a hog?

418
00:28:42.846 --> 00:28:45.265
You should… take the GED.

419
00:28:46.683 --> 00:28:47.976
I'll work at the factory.

420
00:28:58.445 --> 00:29:01.030
Do you know the reason
I'm going to marry Yang Gwan-sik,

421
00:29:01.114 --> 00:29:03.199
the least cool boy in all of Jeju?

422
00:29:07.412 --> 00:29:08.496
You are

423
00:29:10.081 --> 00:29:11.040
like steel.

424
00:29:14.127 --> 00:29:17.338
We may get hungry,
but you'll never break my heart.

425
00:29:21.259 --> 00:29:23.928
Even if I was given
a gold or a silver axe,

426
00:29:24.012 --> 00:29:25.722
I would choose the steel axe.

427
00:29:26.306 --> 00:29:27.849
The steel one's useful.

428
00:29:29.350 --> 00:29:31.895
Nobody would give you
a gold or silver axe anyway.

429
00:29:32.479 --> 00:29:35.899
Yeah, the least cool boy I know.

430
00:29:47.202 --> 00:29:48.495
You said we're married.

431
00:29:51.831 --> 00:29:53.124
Seems like we're not.

432
00:29:57.587 --> 00:29:59.547
Uh, It doesn't seem like it at all now.

433
00:30:07.430 --> 00:30:08.515
Yang Gwan-sik.

434
00:30:13.436 --> 00:30:15.188
Excuse me.

435
00:30:25.949 --> 00:30:27.116
Jeez.

436
00:30:27.867 --> 00:30:30.453
Why are you giddy
when she ripped off your rings?

437
00:30:30.537 --> 00:30:33.248
She, uh, did swipe
your yellow dress, right?

438
00:30:34.582 --> 00:30:36.876
You know, the boy's family,

439
00:30:37.377 --> 00:30:41.130
Gwan-sik, right?
At his house, their gold frog is gone.

440
00:30:41.673 --> 00:30:44.384
She poached their gold frog
and their son too.

441
00:30:47.136 --> 00:30:49.556
You're so giddy. Is this fun for you?

442
00:30:50.890 --> 00:30:53.852
The kid's grandma,
see, she almost fainted.

443
00:30:53.935 --> 00:30:55.979
Man, oh man, they're rash.

444
00:30:56.062 --> 00:30:58.481
How'd they imagine
running off to Busan like that?

445
00:30:58.565 --> 00:31:01.776
But rumor has it, they may have
caused a riot on that boat.

446
00:31:04.112 --> 00:31:07.282
They've been saying
that Ae-sun was behind the whole thing.

447
00:31:07.365 --> 00:31:09.075
Jeez.

448
00:31:11.077 --> 00:31:13.746
Ae-sun is a romantic, huh?

449
00:31:13.830 --> 00:31:17.584
- Well, come on, they're lovers on the run.
- What's the point of it all?

450
00:31:17.667 --> 00:31:18.668
Who cares about romance?

451
00:31:18.751 --> 00:31:21.462
Once food becomes a problem,
then they'll start to hate each other.

452
00:31:22.046 --> 00:31:23.798
What's being hungry at that age, huh?

453
00:31:23.882 --> 00:31:27.510
Right now, even if all day,
they just eat tangerines together

454
00:31:27.594 --> 00:31:30.346
on a cold marble floor,
they'd still be happy.

455
00:31:31.806 --> 00:31:32.640
Min-ok.

456
00:31:34.934 --> 00:31:35.768
Were you happy?

457
00:31:36.561 --> 00:31:39.188
I've never eaten tangerines with you,
my dear.

458
00:31:41.524 --> 00:31:42.400
Now we could.

459
00:31:44.068 --> 00:31:45.153
Anyone home?

460
00:31:49.365 --> 00:31:51.242
Write down the outfit
you think she wore, okay?

461
00:31:51.993 --> 00:31:55.079
- Evidently, she stole your clothes.
- Are you going after them?

462
00:31:55.580 --> 00:31:57.874
You're like a bounty hunter.
That's so cool.

463
00:31:58.583 --> 00:32:01.794
How will you find them?
You never will. You never will.

464
00:32:02.962 --> 00:32:05.131
Stop talking and write it down now.

465
00:32:05.715 --> 00:32:08.009
- I don't know what she wore.
- What?

466
00:32:08.092 --> 00:32:11.429
I sell fashion door-to-door.
I have so many clothes.

467
00:32:12.055 --> 00:32:13.765
Damn it.

468
00:32:13.848 --> 00:32:15.058
Oh man.

469
00:32:15.141 --> 00:32:17.101
It's their first night, probably.

470
00:32:17.936 --> 00:32:20.188
- Ah.
- Shut up.

471
00:32:22.440 --> 00:32:24.651
Busan's hospitality is top-notch.

472
00:32:25.985 --> 00:32:28.655
This is Busan's crown jewel.

473
00:32:28.738 --> 00:32:29.864
It'd be a shame

474
00:32:30.531 --> 00:32:32.367
for you to miss tasting a bit.

475
00:32:34.827 --> 00:32:37.288
Is this all free of charge?

476
00:32:38.331 --> 00:32:40.458
Busan is a huge city.

477
00:32:42.085 --> 00:32:43.544
The floor's all warm now.

478
00:32:44.128 --> 00:32:47.715
So just finish drinking the soju
and get some sleep, all right?

479
00:32:48.299 --> 00:32:50.385
If both of you lie down
on this nice warm floor,

480
00:32:50.468 --> 00:32:54.597
then you will melt like
a little butter in a frying pan.

481
00:32:55.139 --> 00:32:57.934
But before you melt on the floor…

482
00:33:00.311 --> 00:33:01.604
…take your time

483
00:33:01.688 --> 00:33:03.314
and enjoy

484
00:33:03.940 --> 00:33:04.774
your night.

485
00:33:06.943 --> 00:33:09.529
Oh, well, it is your honeymoon, after all.

486
00:33:11.698 --> 00:33:15.368
Oh dear, you're both flushed.
Please just get right to it.

487
00:33:15.451 --> 00:33:17.704
You're in the best place
for a night like this.

488
00:33:17.787 --> 00:33:21.290
Here, even the most unschooled men
learn everything there is to know.

489
00:33:21.374 --> 00:33:22.542
Stop it, miss.

490
00:33:23.668 --> 00:33:24.794
Oh dear.

491
00:33:24.877 --> 00:33:25.753
Please just stop.

492
00:33:32.719 --> 00:33:33.553
Give it everything.

493
00:33:50.153 --> 00:33:51.529
<i>Give it everything.</i>

494
00:33:53.698 --> 00:33:55.241
<i>Give it everything.</i>

495
00:34:09.672 --> 00:34:13.009
<i>Jaecheop-guk </i>for sale. <i>Jaecheop-guk.</i>

496
00:34:14.969 --> 00:34:18.264
<i>Jaecheop-guk </i>for sale. <i>Jaecheop-guk.</i>

497
00:34:31.569 --> 00:34:32.904
Is the toilet clean?

498
00:34:33.905 --> 00:34:34.739
Huh?

499
00:34:35.406 --> 00:34:36.240
Yeah.

500
00:34:37.283 --> 00:34:38.534
It's completely fine.

501
00:34:40.953 --> 00:34:41.788
Huh?

502
00:34:42.371 --> 00:34:43.581
Did you break the fan?

503
00:34:46.918 --> 00:34:47.752
Huh?

504
00:34:53.091 --> 00:34:54.759
Um, maybe a screw fell out.

505
00:34:56.177 --> 00:34:58.971
Well, just leave it, then.

506
00:34:59.555 --> 00:35:02.183
- Okay?
- Okay. But what if they charge us for it?

507
00:35:02.683 --> 00:35:05.812
But see, Busan's hospitality is top-notch.

508
00:35:21.410 --> 00:35:22.328
BILL
TOTAL: 640 WON

509
00:35:23.788 --> 00:35:26.040
Didn't she say all that stuff
she gave us was on the house?

510
00:35:26.124 --> 00:35:28.376
Hmm.

511
00:35:29.127 --> 00:35:31.629
Ow. What's this?

512
00:35:32.130 --> 00:35:32.964
What's this?

513
00:35:34.382 --> 00:35:35.633
Ow, that hurt.

514
00:35:46.894 --> 00:35:48.146
What's going on?

515
00:35:52.150 --> 00:35:53.609
What? What is it?

516
00:35:55.695 --> 00:35:58.406
What? What's going on, hmm?

517
00:35:58.489 --> 00:36:00.199
- Our suitcase.
- Hmm?

518
00:36:00.283 --> 00:36:02.118
- Where's our suitcase?
- Suitcase?

519
00:36:04.370 --> 00:36:05.997
<i>Were any other rooms robbed?</i>

520
00:36:06.080 --> 00:36:07.832
Were there guests
who seemed strange?

521
00:36:07.915 --> 00:36:10.251
- What are you suggesting, miss?
- What?

522
00:36:11.794 --> 00:36:13.546
Stop playing around and pay up.

523
00:36:13.629 --> 00:36:16.799
The charges are for room service
and for breaking the fan mount.

524
00:36:16.883 --> 00:36:20.219
The broken mount is the evidence.
Why would it be broken though?

525
00:36:20.303 --> 00:36:22.555
- The thief was tip-toeing in the dark.
- Stop!

526
00:36:23.848 --> 00:36:26.434
You guys broke the fan.
I know it was you two.

527
00:36:26.517 --> 00:36:28.311
- Why would we do it?
- Well, hold on.

528
00:36:28.394 --> 00:36:30.229
Look, it's possible
your guests saw something.

529
00:36:30.313 --> 00:36:31.397
- Maybe we could ask.
- Mm-hmm.

530
00:36:31.480 --> 00:36:33.691
Let's call ourselves
the hotel where they rob guests.

531
00:36:33.774 --> 00:36:35.359
Ah, maybe your wife saw something.

532
00:36:35.443 --> 00:36:36.944
- Yeah.
- Sorry?

533
00:36:37.570 --> 00:36:39.780
I never saw you with any bag at all.

534
00:36:40.489 --> 00:36:43.701
- I remember you came here empty-handed.
- And you will sit right here.

535
00:36:44.243 --> 00:36:45.620
- Hey.
- Yeah?

536
00:36:45.703 --> 00:36:48.289
Did you see these people
bring a suitcase with them?

537
00:36:48.873 --> 00:36:49.916
Mm-mm.

538
00:36:49.999 --> 00:36:51.584
Ah, what?

539
00:36:52.293 --> 00:36:54.962
Oh, this came from the suitcase we had.

540
00:36:55.546 --> 00:36:57.632
- But it was left on the floor.
- Wow!

541
00:36:57.715 --> 00:37:00.384
You didn't even have a suitcase,
so we took pity on you kids.

542
00:37:00.468 --> 00:37:01.969
Now you want us to give you one?

543
00:37:02.053 --> 00:37:05.181
No. No, we set our suitcase
by this window.

544
00:37:05.264 --> 00:37:07.850
- You gave me the key.
- You must be so upset.

545
00:37:08.851 --> 00:37:09.727
Right, well,

546
00:37:10.603 --> 00:37:11.729
why don't we call the police?

547
00:37:12.605 --> 00:37:13.814
Should we call them

548
00:37:14.357 --> 00:37:16.734
and tell them
that these kids here are runaways?

549
00:37:17.318 --> 00:37:20.071
Busan's hospitality
is top-notch, huh?

550
00:37:20.613 --> 00:37:22.865
This is Busan's crown jewel.

551
00:37:22.949 --> 00:37:25.743
It'd be such a shame
if you didn't get to taste this.

552
00:37:32.667 --> 00:37:33.501
MISSING PERSONS

553
00:37:33.584 --> 00:37:35.294
YANG GWAN-SIK, MALE, AGE 19
HANDSOME

554
00:37:35.378 --> 00:37:37.088
OH AE-SUN, FEMALE, AGE 18
VIXEN-LIKE

555
00:37:38.130 --> 00:37:39.006
Yes.

556
00:37:43.636 --> 00:37:44.512
Look, ma'am,

557
00:37:44.595 --> 00:37:47.056
you may as well search
for them at Jagalchi Market.

558
00:37:47.139 --> 00:37:50.643
How in the world will you find kids
who were so determined to run away?

559
00:37:51.894 --> 00:37:56.607
I'm running out of time, Mother.
Enough about your dreams already.

560
00:37:56.691 --> 00:37:58.609
I've gotta go, okay?

561
00:37:59.610 --> 00:38:00.528
Dream reading?

562
00:38:04.365 --> 00:38:07.285
And why'd the rooster snatch the kids?

563
00:38:08.077 --> 00:38:11.247
Are you telling me
you'd like some chicken for supper?

564
00:38:11.330 --> 00:38:13.040
Cock-a-doodle-doo.

565
00:38:13.124 --> 00:38:14.417
Newlyweds, huh?

566
00:38:14.500 --> 00:38:17.003
Here's the fried chicken
you ordered.

567
00:38:17.086 --> 00:38:18.462
Enjoy your meal!

568
00:38:18.546 --> 00:38:20.631
Do you take me for a moron? Huh?

569
00:38:20.715 --> 00:38:22.591
You really thought you had me fooled?

570
00:38:22.675 --> 00:38:24.844
Why did you give us a room and alcohol?

571
00:38:24.927 --> 00:38:27.847
- Without bags or any money at all?
- Stop yapping.

572
00:38:28.556 --> 00:38:30.266
Let's call the police now.

573
00:38:30.349 --> 00:38:34.020
Let's call the cops and have your mother
come by boat from Jeju.

574
00:38:34.103 --> 00:38:35.813
I should break this girl's legs, damn it.

575
00:38:35.896 --> 00:38:37.606
How did you know
we're from Jeju?

576
00:38:43.195 --> 00:38:44.363
Get out. Yeah, go.

577
00:38:44.447 --> 00:38:46.907
- I'll just pretend it's bad luck. Go!
- Wait a minute.

578
00:38:47.408 --> 00:38:49.618
How did you know we're from Jeju? How?

579
00:38:50.911 --> 00:38:53.706
Shall I call the police?
How about we argue over every detail?

580
00:38:53.789 --> 00:38:54.665
Boarding passes.

581
00:38:55.458 --> 00:38:57.585
I know you robbed us.
They were in our bag.

582
00:38:59.253 --> 00:39:00.087
You idiot.

583
00:39:00.838 --> 00:39:01.964
You idiot.

584
00:39:03.549 --> 00:39:04.717
Oh, my bag.

585
00:39:05.593 --> 00:39:06.427
Oh.

586
00:39:07.011 --> 00:39:08.471
Our suitcase, wow.

587
00:39:08.554 --> 00:39:09.722
Give it back.

588
00:39:10.598 --> 00:39:12.558
Oh, that suitcase is all we have left.

589
00:39:13.851 --> 00:39:16.771
Oh, my mom's picture is in that suitcase.

590
00:39:16.854 --> 00:39:19.190
Oh, my suitcase.

591
00:39:20.775 --> 00:39:23.694
You kept making the room hotter.
Then you kept giving us drinks.

592
00:39:24.278 --> 00:39:27.448
You made sure we were fast asleep
to be able to steal our suitcase.

593
00:39:27.531 --> 00:39:29.950
Wait, all the towels
they have were stolen too.

594
00:39:30.034 --> 00:39:32.495
SUBONGYONG SAUNA
NAMPO BARBERSHOP - JUNGANG SAUNA

595
00:39:33.245 --> 00:39:34.455
You thieves.

596
00:39:35.081 --> 00:39:36.415
You… you thieves.

597
00:39:37.666 --> 00:39:39.001
You have evidence?

598
00:39:39.835 --> 00:39:42.463
- The boarding passes! You saw them.
- So what if we did?

599
00:39:42.546 --> 00:39:44.715
- Where's the evidence?
- Where's the evidence?

600
00:39:45.966 --> 00:39:47.635
Leave while
we're still being nice.

601
00:39:48.511 --> 00:39:51.722
You know, before we sell the both of you.

602
00:39:53.015 --> 00:39:54.683
Leave while
we're still being nice.

603
00:39:57.937 --> 00:40:00.314
The suitcase was all we had.

604
00:40:03.567 --> 00:40:05.903
That was the only picture of Mom I had.

605
00:40:08.114 --> 00:40:10.324
The gold frog was in there too.

606
00:40:12.410 --> 00:40:14.662
That's what we get for begging.

607
00:40:16.080 --> 00:40:18.249
The same as
those little storybook children

608
00:40:18.332 --> 00:40:22.128
who were beguiled by breadcrumbs
and captured by a witch.

609
00:40:24.046 --> 00:40:24.964
I don't know them.

610
00:40:26.715 --> 00:40:28.175
<i>Hansel and Gretel.</i>

611
00:40:29.844 --> 00:40:31.011
Never heard of it.

612
00:40:34.056 --> 00:40:38.185
Oh, well, I always thought those kids
were the biggest morons.

613
00:40:38.853 --> 00:40:40.813
They shoved candy in their mouths

614
00:40:41.730 --> 00:40:44.525
with no clue about
how close they were to being eaten.

615
00:40:50.072 --> 00:40:51.490
What happened to those kids?

616
00:40:52.450 --> 00:40:53.284
Did they live?

617
00:40:54.326 --> 00:40:55.619
They killed her.

618
00:40:56.996 --> 00:40:59.165
- She killed the kids?
- No.

619
00:41:00.040 --> 00:41:01.834
They killed <i>her</i>.

620
00:41:05.296 --> 00:41:07.089
The children pushed the witch…

621
00:41:09.091 --> 00:41:10.551
…into an oven, and…

622
00:41:11.635 --> 00:41:13.637
and they burned her alive.

623
00:41:14.722 --> 00:41:15.556
Ae-sun.

624
00:41:16.056 --> 00:41:17.516
They killed her,

625
00:41:18.350 --> 00:41:21.437
took all her silver,
gold, and all her treasures,

626
00:41:22.688 --> 00:41:25.316
and they lived happily ever after.

627
00:41:27.067 --> 00:41:27.985
Uh, Ae-sun…

628
00:41:28.486 --> 00:41:30.529
They really were something.

629
00:41:47.254 --> 00:41:49.798
It's all on the house. All free.

630
00:41:49.882 --> 00:41:51.717
Busan's hospitality is top-notch.

631
00:41:51.800 --> 00:41:54.386
Drink all of that in this warm room,

632
00:41:54.470 --> 00:41:58.140
and you'll melt on the floor
like butter in a frying pan.

633
00:41:59.183 --> 00:42:02.937
- This and this and this right here.
- Oh, what happened to your fan?

634
00:42:03.979 --> 00:42:05.898
Damn it! It happened yesterday.

635
00:42:05.981 --> 00:42:09.276
Lunatics got in,
making a total mess of the place.

636
00:42:10.986 --> 00:42:12.613
Hurry. Let me climb on your back.

637
00:42:12.696 --> 00:42:14.281
- Oh, okay.
- Hurry.

638
00:42:14.365 --> 00:42:17.993
Ah, these kids came in here
and made us so mad.

639
00:42:18.077 --> 00:42:20.538
I wanted to strangle them,
but I let them go.

640
00:42:21.205 --> 00:42:22.957
We're all polite here, you know?

641
00:42:47.398 --> 00:42:48.524
What is it?

642
00:42:50.901 --> 00:42:52.027
Excuse us.

643
00:42:53.696 --> 00:42:55.406
I think I've had enough freebies.

644
00:42:55.489 --> 00:42:58.242
- Those "free things"?
- If you get drunk, they'll rob you.

645
00:42:58.325 --> 00:43:00.786
She said to drink it all
and melt like butter, right?

646
00:43:01.579 --> 00:43:02.454
Who are you guys?

647
00:43:02.538 --> 00:43:05.457
Listen. Just don't
turn off the lights, okay?

648
00:43:22.516 --> 00:43:24.101
Why isn't she sleeping?

649
00:43:26.937 --> 00:43:28.188
Hey, bug.

650
00:43:33.027 --> 00:43:34.903
Well, we're not making money tonight.

651
00:43:36.864 --> 00:43:38.616
Charge her double for soju tomorrow.

652
00:43:39.116 --> 00:43:39.950
Oh man.

653
00:43:42.328 --> 00:43:43.329
Oh man.

654
00:43:54.423 --> 00:43:57.009
The gold frog
and Mom's picture is priority. Got it?

655
00:43:58.802 --> 00:44:00.554
We look for our stuff first,

656
00:44:00.638 --> 00:44:03.182
and if we can't find it,
we take their cash box, okay?

657
00:44:07.561 --> 00:44:10.522
We'd be at a loss still.
Frog's worth more than their box.

658
00:44:11.106 --> 00:44:12.524
You see, we're not stealing.

659
00:44:18.822 --> 00:44:21.408
We need our things
to live together, right?

660
00:44:24.078 --> 00:44:25.079
Gwan-sik.

661
00:44:26.163 --> 00:44:28.332
You must be the head of the house, 'kay?

662
00:44:35.756 --> 00:44:37.675
Baby.

663
00:44:43.013 --> 00:44:43.972
Baby.

664
00:44:50.396 --> 00:44:51.230
Let's go.

665
00:45:20.259 --> 00:45:21.593
It's not there.

666
00:45:22.136 --> 00:45:23.053
Not there.

667
00:45:38.068 --> 00:45:39.653
Hey. Hey.

668
00:45:39.737 --> 00:45:40.612
Don't open it.

669
00:45:40.696 --> 00:45:41.905
Don't open it.

670
00:45:41.989 --> 00:45:43.657
Cash. Cash. Cash.

671
00:45:44.324 --> 00:45:45.325
Cashbox.

672
00:46:21.236 --> 00:46:22.237
Got it.

673
00:46:43.967 --> 00:46:47.513
Let's just go.
Go. I'll get you a new one.

674
00:46:58.941 --> 00:47:00.150
Run! Come on!

675
00:47:03.487 --> 00:47:04.822
Hey! Stop!

676
00:47:05.697 --> 00:47:07.866
- Stop!
- Hey!

677
00:47:08.951 --> 00:47:09.952
The cashbox.

678
00:47:10.452 --> 00:47:12.246
- Lady!
- Put it down.

679
00:47:12.830 --> 00:47:15.290
- Right. 24 seconds. 24 seconds.
- Put down the cashbox.

680
00:47:15.374 --> 00:47:17.376
- Damn it, you asshole.
- Put down the cashbox.

681
00:47:17.459 --> 00:47:19.086
I swear I'll beat this girl to a pulp.

682
00:47:21.171 --> 00:47:22.589
I'm done for.

683
00:47:22.673 --> 00:47:23.674
Oh, just go.

684
00:47:23.757 --> 00:47:25.843
Go! Just go!

685
00:47:25.926 --> 00:47:28.929
You want us to sell this girl? Huh?
Somewhere she won't be found?

686
00:47:31.515 --> 00:47:32.850
That's the pit of my stomach.

687
00:47:34.601 --> 00:47:36.478
My stomach, my stomach.

688
00:47:36.562 --> 00:47:38.063
Put it down before I lose it.

689
00:47:38.564 --> 00:47:41.024
- Come at me. Let's do it.
- Put it down, damn it!

690
00:47:46.697 --> 00:47:49.032
- Okay, let up a bit. I'm dying.
- Quiet, you.

691
00:47:49.116 --> 00:47:51.368
Damn it. Put it down. Now!

692
00:47:51.451 --> 00:47:53.328
- Lady, lady.
- Look at that punk.

693
00:47:54.079 --> 00:47:55.622
Yeah. Just go.

694
00:47:56.206 --> 00:47:58.417
- Put it down.
- Yeah, run along, asshole.

695
00:47:58.500 --> 00:48:00.961
Go, go, asshole. Go.

696
00:48:02.880 --> 00:48:04.089
That damn punk.

697
00:48:05.674 --> 00:48:07.509
I said, put it down, you scum!

698
00:48:08.886 --> 00:48:10.762
That's right. There you go.

699
00:48:11.471 --> 00:48:13.974
What the…
what the hell is he doing? What?

700
00:48:22.566 --> 00:48:26.403
<i>Mom's first love</i>
<i>was the karate master Choi Bae-dal.</i>

701
00:48:28.780 --> 00:48:29.823
<i>And Mom</i>

702
00:48:29.907 --> 00:48:31.533
<i>was "Headbutting" Kim Il.</i>

703
00:51:24.372 --> 00:51:29.002
"THE SAME SKY, THE SAME STARS,
ETCHED IN THE SAME HEARTS"

